    <string name="ecg_explain_sinus">Your heart beat in a uniform pattern between 50 and 100 bpm. This is the pattern usually seen in a normally beating heart.</string>
    <string name="ecg_explain_afib">Your heart beat in an irregular pattern. This can be a sign of atrial fibrillation (AFib). If you haven\'t been told you have AFib, talk to your doctor.</string>
    <string name="ecg_explain_high_hr">Your heart rate was over 120 bpm, so the rhythm couldn\'t be checked. Exercise, stress, alcohol or dehydration can raise your heart rate.</string>
    <string name="ecg_explain_low_hr">Your heart rate was under 50 bpm, so the rhythm couldn\'t be checked. Some medicines and very good fitness can lower your heart rate.</string>
    <string name="ecg_explain_inconclusive">The recording couldn\'t be classified. Make sure your arm is resting and try again.</string>
    <string name="ecg_explain_poor">Too much noise was detected. Rest your arm on a table, keep still and touch the key lightly.</string>

