    <string name="about_spo2">Blood oxygen is measured with red and infrared light while you keep still. Readings of 95–100% are typical at rest. It isn\'t a medical oximeter.</string>
    <string name="about_temp">Skin temperature changes with the room and your activity, so Heartline shows the change from your own 7-day baseline. It isn\'t body temperature.</string>
    <string name="about_body">Body composition uses a small electrical current between your wrist and fingers. Measure at the same time of day, before eating or exercising.</string>
    <string name="about_stress">Stress is estimated from your heart rate variability over one minute at rest (and skin conductance on Galaxy Watch8). Lower is calmer.</string>
    <string name="profile_hint">Used to personalise Heartline and to estimate body composition on your watch. It stays on your devices.</string>
